From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32, ntdll, server: RegReplaceKey

The stub did nothing and said it succeeded (MediaInfo imports it). As on Windows: the file a loaded
hive came from becomes the backup and the new file takes its name, so the next load of the hive has
the new keys (the hive in memory stays as it is); SeRestorePrivilege needed. The server remembers the
file of a hive loaded with NtLoadKey (get_hive_file). Wine's own registry files hold many of Windows'
hives together and are not replaced. Gate: test/regreplace-gate.sh. Mutant: SG_MUTANT_NO_HIVE_FILE.
---
--- a/server/registry.c
+++ b/server/registry.c
@@ -101,6 +101,8 @@
